---
// SolarAlignmentGuide.astro - Sun & Shadow Method with dark mode support
---

<section id="section-solar" class="scroll-mt-20 py-6 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto w-full">
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626] bg-white dark:bg-[#121212] p-6 shadow-[0_0_0_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.06),0px_2px_4px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)]">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
      <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-950 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 text-sm">☀️</span>
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white">
        Sun & Shadow Alignment Method (Magnetic-Proof)
      </h2>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1] leading-relaxed mb-5">
      Phone magnetometers can be skewed by indoor iron rebar, laptops, and speakers. By comparing the sun's real-time astronomical azimuth with the Qibla bearing, you can align with 100% physical precision.
    </p>

    <!-- 2 Column Layout -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 items-center">
      <!-- Left: Real-time Solar Angle vs Qibla Box -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626] bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[#171717] p-4 flex flex-col justify-between h-full">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono font-medium text-[#888888] dark:text-[#737373] uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2">Live Solar Coordinates</span>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="rounded-md bg-white dark:bg-[#121212] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626] p-3 text-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-[#888888] dark:text-[#737373] block">Sun Azimuth</span>
              <span id="guide-sun-azimuth" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white block">--°</span>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-md bg-white dark:bg-[#121212] border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#262626] p-3 text-center">
              <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-[#888888] dark:text-[#737373] block">Sun Elevation</span>
              <span id="guide-sun-altitude" class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-white block">--°</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="guide-sun-instruction-box" class="rounded-md bg-amber-50/80 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800 p-3 text-xs text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200">
          <strong class="font-semibold block mb-0.5">Real-Time Solar Rule:</strong>
          <span id="guide-sun-diff-text">Calculating sun relative angle...</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: Step-by-Step Practical Steps -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#171717] dark:bg-white text-[11px] font-mono text-white dark:text-[#171717] font-semibold">1</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
            <strong>Place a vertical object</strong> (e.g. bottle or pencil) on flat ground exposed to sunlight or window shadow.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#171717] dark:bg-white text-[11px] font-mono text-white dark:text-[#171717] font-semibold">2</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
            <strong>Identify shadow direction:</strong> The shadow points directly opposite to the Sun Azimuth (180° away from the sun).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#171717] dark:bg-white text-[11px] font-mono text-white dark:text-[#171717] font-semibold">3</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1]">
            <strong>Turn by the relative angle</strong> displayed above from the sun/shadow line to face the exact Holy Kaaba.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
